Z||000000||Monkeyman||08-16-2001||12:01 PM||||No.  I didn't win the lottery, but the multi state Powerball is up to 120 million bucks.  I had some extra time on my hands last night (had to train a new clerk in) and got thinking about how much that jackpot is really worth.  I hear everyday that "you can't really make it on less than 100 million.  (Whatever!)  Here's how I figure the math:<P>If you take the cash option, you'll get approximately half of the total jackpot ($60 million).  Uncle Sam will take 1/3 in taxes (assuming you live in the States) which leaves $40.2 million clear.  If you take $10.2 million out of that (gotta buy more Fieros, houses, pay off credit cards, give some away, etc), that leaves $30 million to put in the bank.  Don't touch the money for one year.  Even at 5% interest, one years interest would be $1.5 million.  Only take out one weeks interest at a time.  That's $28,846.15 (each week for the rest of your life!!).  After Uncle Sam takes his 33%, you're still left with $19,326.92 <B>after taxes</B> !!!  The weekly interest will grow every week as you'll be collecting interest (the second week) on $31,471,153.85 instead of the original $30 million.<P>A dozen people in the last 18 hours have swore that they couldn't live on that.  Could you????? <P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000001||JSocha||08-16-2001||12:04 PM||||&lt;said in an arrogant, pompas rich voice, Harvard style&gt;<P>I don't know.  With my lavish lifestyle, I guess it would depend on the call girls going rates. &lt;takes a delicate sip of his Champaign&gt;<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000002||The Fieromaster||08-16-2001||12:44 PM||||WOW with $19,326.92 a WEEK I could move outta my cardboard box... or a LEAST get one thats wax covered!  Maybe a add on garage for the Fiero!!<P><FONT SIZE="3"><B>HELL YEA</B></FONT> I could live on that much a week!!  Figure some people live on that much a YEAR!!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">         <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">      <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">                 <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B><BR><p>[This message has been edited by The Fieromaster (edited 08-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||08-16-2001||12:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>Only take out one weeks interest at a time.  [snip]  The weekly interest will grow every week as you'll be collecting interest (the second week) on $31,471,153.85 instead of the original $30 million.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, your intrest won't grow, and the original $30M won't get any larger, if you take out each week's interest every week. But you'll still have that $19K per week income (after taxes) to play with, but it won't get any bigger unless you invest some of it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||IwannaIRM||08-16-2001||01:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR>Here's how I figure the math:<P><B>If you take the cash option, you'll get approximately half of the total jackpot ($60 million).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Roughly, based on actual money in lottery's till at the time, amount could be higher or lower.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>Uncle Sam will take 1/3 in taxes (assuming you live in the States) which leaves $40.2 million clear.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Actually, feds will take 20% one time flat tax and your state will take their applicable tax.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>If you take $10.2 million out of that (gotta buy more Fieros, houses, pay off credit cards, give some away, etc), that leaves $30 million to put in the bank.  Don't touch the money for one year.  Even at 5% interest, one years interest would be $1.5 million.  Only take out one weeks interest at a time.  That's $28,846.15 (each week for the rest of your life!!).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Well, if you don't touch the money for a year you will have 31.5m in the bank and you will draw interest the second year on that amount.  So you would roughly get $30,288.46 each week.  But your balance of $31.5m wouldn't change.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>After Uncle Sam takes his 33%, you're still left with $19,326.92 [b]after taxes</B>!!![/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Uncle Sam won't continue to take out 33% per year.  You will only pay tax on unearned income which is at a lower tax rate.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>The weekly interest will grow every week as you'll be collecting interest (the second week) on $31,471,153.85 instead of the original $30 million.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Actually your weekly interest would not change if you keep taking it out.  You will only be earning interest on your "untouched" balance.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>A dozen people in the last 18 hours have swore that they couldn't live on that.  Could you?????</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Hmm, that's a tough one...Oh you bet I could live on that amount a week, no matter who's doing the math.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR><P>------------------<BR>AIM - SWags2933<P>84 Fiero SE (being modified)<BR>88 Formula||||reg||1
