Z||000011||Black88GT||08-16-2001||01:59 PM||||You remember the saying, if it sounds to good to be true, it probably is?  Well that applies to these bank interest schemes people think of when dreaming of winning the lottery.  <P>If you were to have 30 mil. sitting in your hands, you can't just walk into a bank and say "yeah I wanna open up a savings account".  You will have to set up a special meeting with all kinds of chairmen and VIPs about putting your money in their bank.  The chances of getting a 5% interest rate is next to impossible.  Remember, they do this for a living, they aren't dumb, they know what you could make off their interest too.  You would be lucky to get 1-2%.  Not to mention you would probably have to hire a lawyer to be on the safe side or to write up some type of contract, he will cost you some money too.  Then don't forget about the Gold Club!||||reg||1
